# Known MODERATE/HIGH/CRITICAL npm advisories in integrations/agent-guard/package-lock.json.
# Read by gate.mjs in the CI supply-chain job. One `GHSA-id@package` per line
# (the advisory in that package only); the rest of the line is a note. A new
# advisory at moderate or above fails CI; so does a listed one that is no
# longer reported (prune it in the change that fixes it).
#
# Recorded 2026-10-02 (R-P8 phase 3): 0 critical and 0 high. This is the
# package that holds the signing key in every integration; it does not depend
# on solana-agent-kit, so the bigint-buffer advisory is not in it.
#
# Re-recorded 2026-10-20, when the gate began to fail on moderate advisories
# too: `npm audit` reports 4 moderate, all through jayson 4.3.0, the HTTP
# JSON-RPC client of @solana/web3.js 1.x. web3.js loads only
# `jayson/lib/client/browser`, which requires `uuid` (v4) and
# `generateRequest` and nothing else. They go when the guard stops using
# @solana/web3.js 1.x (its transactions are already compiled and signed by
# @solana/kit; the Connection and the public types remain); npm's only offered
# fix is web3.js 3.x, a major across the guard's public types.
#
# Re-checked 2026-10-21 (Round 30): the same four, same path; each entry now
# carries a review-by date the gate enforces.
GHSA-528h-pc64-c93x@stream-json  review-by:2027-01-20  # moderate  stream-json <=3.4.0: pick/ignore/filter/replace filters are O(depth^2) (DoS). stream-json is required only by jayson/lib/utils.js (its server-side request stream parser), which the browser client web3.js loads never requires: the guard process never loads stream-json.
GHSA-hqr4-qq8f-hg3x@stream-json  review-by:2027-01-20  # moderate  stream-json <=3.5.0: the JSONC parser re-scans accumulated comments per chunk (DoS). Same path as above: never loaded by the guard.
GHSA-mjw6-4jj6-33hc@stream-json  review-by:2027-01-20  # moderate  stream-json <3.6.0: prototype pollution in Assembler (this.current[this.key] on plain objects). The serious one of the three, in a process holding a key — and the reason moderate is now gated. Same path as above: jayson's client never requires stream-json, so no RPC answer reaches Assembler.
GHSA-w5hq-g745-h8pq@uuid  review-by:2027-01-20  # moderate  uuid <11.1.1: missing bounds check in v3/v5/v6 when a caller supplies an output buffer. jayson's client calls uuid.v4() with no buffer, so the unchecked write cannot happen. Forcing uuid across three majors into web3.js was judged riskier than the advisory.
#
# Below the gate's threshold (low): none.
